@1 = ~Rot of Ages~
@2 = ~Rot of Ages
(Necromancy)

Level: 1
Range: Touch
Duration: Special
Casting Time: 1
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: Special

Upon touching the target, the caster causes a mass of rotting vegetation, flesh, and other decaying organic matter to erupt around and envelop the creature. The target is blinded for 1 round with no save. The target must then make a Saving Throw vs. Death. On a failed save, it contracts a supernatural disease that inflicts 1 point of poison damage per round for 1 round per caster level, to a maximum of 10 rounds.

If Rot of Ages is cast again upon a creature already suffering from this disease and the target fails its Saving Throw again, the new infection stacks with the previous one, and the target becomes nauseated for 2 rounds. A creature that succeeds on its Saving Throw does not contract the disease and is therefore not considered to be suffering from Rot of Ages for the purpose of subsequent applications.~

// Combat log
@3 = ~Blinded by Rot of Ages~
@4 = ~Diseased by Rot of Ages~
@5 = ~Nauseated by Rot of Ages~
